wifi: brcmfmac: do not wait for an ACK of group-addressed action frames

The firmware completes every action frame with
BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_COMPLETE and reports a group-addressed frame,
which is never acknowledged, with BRCMF_E_STATUS_NO_ACK.
brcmf_p2p_notify_action_tx_complete() takes that as a failed
transmission, so brcmf_p2p_send_action_frame() retries the frame up to
P2P_AF_TX_MAX_RETRY times and finally reports it to cfg80211 as not
acknowledged although it was sent every time. This affects broadcast
frames such as DPP presence announcements and vendor-specific Public
Action frames.

Treat NO_ACK for a group-addressed destination as a successful
transmission.

On a CYW43455 (firmware 7.45.265, Raspberry Pi 3B+) the firmware
reported NO_ACK for 300 of 300 broadcast action frames that a peer
received. With this change, NL80211_CMD_FRAME reports 100 of 100
broadcast frames as sent, each transmitted once.

Tool use: this change was prepared with the help of an AI coding
assistant (Claude), which read the driver, wrote the change and the
changelog, and ran the test described in the cover letter; the
submitter reviewed and tested it.

(Upstream series for wireless-next, carried in Splanc's Pi images: pi/provisioning/nix/brcmfmac-actframe.nix.)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
index ac5ecda6c..37cf6549e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
@@ -1536,7 +1536,12 @@ int brcmf_p2p_notify_action_tx_complete(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 		return 0;
 
 	if (e->event_code == BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_COMPLETE) {
-		if (e->status == BRCMF_E_STATUS_SUCCESS) {
+		/* Group-addressed frames are never acknowledged; the firmware
+		 * reports them with BRCMF_E_STATUS_NO_ACK once sent.
+		 */
+		if (e->status == BRCMF_E_STATUS_SUCCESS ||
+		    (e->status == BRCMF_E_STATUS_NO_ACK &&
+		     is_multicast_ether_addr(p2p->afx_hdl.tx_dst_addr))) {
 			set_bit(BRCMF_P2P_STATUS_ACTION_TX_COMPLETED,
 				&p2p->status);
 			if (!p2p->wait_for_offchan_complete)
